/S0377-2217(01)00227-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Snyder</surname><given-names>LV</given-names></name><name><surname>Daskin</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A random-key genetic algorithm for the genralized traveling salesman problem</article-title><source>European Journal of Operational Research</source><year>2006</year><volume>174</volume><fpage>38</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ejor.2004.09.057</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kripfganz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Perlt</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><source>Operations Research 3.1. A Mathematica application package</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Leipzig , SoftAS Gmbh</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pham</surname><given-names>DT</given-names></name><name><surname>Karaboga</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>Intelligent optimization techniques. Genetic algorithms, Tabu search, simulated annealing and neural networks. </source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>London , Springer-Verlag</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nemhauser</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolsey</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><source>Integer and combinatorial optimization</source><year>1999</year><publisher-name>New York , John Wiley &#x00026; Sons</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Simulated Annealing</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cs.sa